From 8f6979e5f932b693e4ffe4da1715021050c74f46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:58:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] lanes: TF_DS_SPEC_SAMPLE (off by default) gives a sampled
 stream speculative sampling - the accept rule over the target's served p and
 the drafter's proposal q, with q's numbers gathered from both ranks at verify

A sampled stream's drafted window is drawn row by row with the stream's key, so its drafts are only ever held for
their confidence: the round keeps a draft only when the target's own sample at its parent row happens to equal it.
Speculative sampling makes the drafter pay for itself: draft x is kept when a tagged uniform falls under
min(1, p(x)/q(x)) over the target's served distribution p and the drafter's proposal q; the first rejection takes a
draw from the residual max(p - q, 0) normalised, which gives x no mass, so the core's acceptPath stops there; with
every draft kept the row after them keeps the target's own draw from p. The seam is verifyFn: rewriting
`o.sampled[r]` is enough, because acceptPath keeps the longest prefix of rows whose tokens match the target's picks.

q. The Markov loop's _score maximises logit + bias (the Markov bias row of the token the step reads: the cached row
when the token has a slot, else the step's staging row), so with T * gumbel(draft key) on the logits the draft is a
draw from q = softmax((logit + bias) / T) over the full vocabulary. A new tf_ds_spec_clean_kernel runs between each
step's _bias and _score (tri_markov.stepsTapped's `mid` hook; the T26 noise kernel, unchanged, runs right after it on
the same rows): it writes each sampled stream's clean scores l = logit + bias into a buffer of its own (`Drafter.sq`,
row stream * block + step) and, after the row's columns, 16 blocks' normaliser partials (the block's largest l and
sum exp((l - max) / T), f32, max-shifted). The host folds every block and rank in double (sampling.foldLse): m = the
row's largest l, lz = ln sum z_b exp((m_b - m) / T), ln q(v) = (l_v - m) / T - lz. Nothing overflows: at a logit of
30 and T = 0.04, exp(l / T) is inf and ln q stays finite. The accept test is in log space (ln u < ln p(x) - ln q(x));
q(x) is read from the same number the residual reads for x's candidate. A row whose numbers are not finite, and the
rows after it, keep the target's own draw (the base rule: exact whatever the drafts).

The pair. The candidates p needs q at are rank 0's (its logits), so the verify cannot carry them. A new frame,
spec_q (kind 16), follows a verify only when rank 0 speculates at least one row: the rows and their global ids (the
target's candidates after top_k/top_p/min_p, then the draft when it is not one). Both ranks derive the same element
list from it (SpecPlan.indices: an id this rank's columns hold, else -1; every row's partials on every rank; padded
to 4), gather their values from `sq` (tf_ds_gather_cols_kernel on absolute indices) and all-gather them once
(Engine.gatherF32: the ring or NCCL, rank r's at r * wide); rank 0 takes the holder's value (the max over the ranks)
and decides (after the sync, a ring collect that gave up ends the round with RingFailed before the values are read).
Every fallible host step (p, the plan) runs before the frame; a follower that cannot join ends. The
drafter pass gains no collective (the normaliser rides the verify's gather), and greedy-only passes and rounds launch
what they did. The pass frames are unchanged: pass_keyed already carries the seeds, now the draft-tagged ones.

The depth. The allocation trims a drafted window by the whole vector of the head's chances, and chance j reads
confidence j, which reads the token step j read (draft j - 1): the choice to verify draft j would hang on draft j
itself through chance j + 1, and the kept drafts would no longer be q's draws. So a speculated stream's
probabilities hook answers false, and the core's per-depth rates trim it (the prior, then the stream's own acceptance
by depth, which the core records every head round: depth.observeDepth).

Keys: the drafter's, the acceptance test's and the residual draw's are three tags mixed into the stream's seed
(sampling.draft_tag, accept_tag, residual_tag), independent of the sampler's own and of each other. TF_DS_SPEC_SAMPLE
parses as the series' switches do (`1` or `on`); TF_DS_T26_KEYED_DRAFT on as ops reads it (exactly `1`) is refused
with it, with a message that says to set TF_DS_T26_KEYED_DRAFT=0. TP2 (or one rank) only: Drafter.init refuses it on
a 2D drafter head or the four-node lane (SpecSampleWorld). The flag is bit 1 of the pair's switches frame and in the
fingerprint's features (`spec_sample=1;`, named only when on). Off: no allocation (the Drafter's new fields are set to
0), no new launch, no new frame, every reply byte for byte the base one; the T26 noise kernel is the base one.

LOSSY, twice. A sampled stream's drafted reply no longer equals its undrafted reply for the same seed: it is the same
distribution (p, per row), not the same tokens. And it is no longer reproducible from its seed alone: the drafts'
depth follows the round loop's allocation and the stream's acceptance history. Greedy streams are untouched: no
noise, no speculation, the same argmax (a sampled round reads its logits on the host with the switch on, so a greedy
stream beside a sampled one takes the host's argmax, as with TF_DS_T27_DEVICE_DRAW off).

Assumed, not seen: _score's arithmetic is logit (fp32) + the fp16 bias row as fp32 (its Triton source is not in this
tree; the recorded launch takes LG fp32, CACHE and STAGE fp16). A tripwire checks it on every speculated row: the
draft must score highest among the gathered ids under clean + T * gumbel(draft key); misses are counted and the first
eight logged ("tripwire misses" on the periodic `dsv41 spec-sample:` line, every 4096 decided rows).

Tests: the rule as implemented reproduces p exactly by enumeration (q's mass on and off p's support, q zero on some
of p's candidates, p == q, disjoint supports); a rejection never emits the draft and a draft off p's support is always
rejected; the emitted token's histogram against p over 200K seeds for one row and a three-draft block, drafts drawn
from q's full support (acceptance sum min(p, q)); the normaliser's host mirror of the kernel (16 blocks of 256 threads,
two ranks) gives q summing to 1 at T = 1 .. 1e-7 where exp(l / T) overflows; the fold skips empty blocks and refuses
non-finite ones; spec_q round-trips, both ranks derive the same count with complementary indices, out-of-bounds frames
are refused; the gather's layout for fewer rows than the bound (rank 1's values at r * wide, not r * max_streams) and
q from it sums to 1; the mid hook's launch order; the keys' independence; the parse and the T26 refusal. The CUDA
path type-checks (`zig build install native -Dfatbins=<dummies>`); the .cu changes were syntax-checked with clang
only. Not run on a pair: tools/samp_test.py (5000 seeds, DRAFTS=0 against the switch on, chi-square of the first and
the conditioned second and third tokens) is the first live gate.
